/**
# Each directory must be un-ignored as well as its contents. `!/src/**` alone does not do it:
# `/**` above matches the bare `src` entry too, so git prunes the directory and never looks
# inside it. Existing files survive only because gitignore does not apply to tracked files --
# which means NEW files added under these directories are silently invisible to `git add`.
# That bit this fork when the first new source file under src/ failed to stage.
!/bin/
!/bin/**
!/cmake/
!/cmake/**
!/etc/
!/etc/**
!/include/
!/include/**
!/media/
!/media/**
# Themes belonging to this fork. NOT dist/themes -- that path is a submodule pointing at a
# third-party repository, so anything added there is invisible to everyone who clones.
!/dist/
!/dist/noggit-themes/
!/dist/noggit-themes/**
!/resources/
!/resources/**
!/sql/
!/sql/**
!/src/
!/src/**
!/test/
!/test/**
!/.idea/**
!.gitignore
!.CMakeLists.txt
!COPYING
!Doxyfile
!README.md
!todo_1.4.md
!uid_fix_concept.md

# --- TrinityCore DB editing (feature/tc335-db-editing) ---
# Line 1 is /** -- this repo ignores everything and whitelists explicitly. Anything not
# un-ignored below is invisible to git, so new top-level directories MUST be added here.
#
# Each directory must be un-ignored as well as its contents. `!/docs/**` alone is not enough:
# `/**` matches the bare `docs` entry too, so git prunes the directory and never looks inside.
# The existing `!/src/**` above only appears to work because src/ is already tracked, and
# gitignore does not apply to tracked files.
!ATTRIBUTION.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
!/tools/
!/tools/**
!/tests/
!/tests/**
# scripts/ holds 23 tracked Lua/TypeScript files inherited from upstream, but was never
# un-ignored -- they survive only because gitignore does not apply to already-tracked files.
# Without this, a NEW file added under scripts/ is silently invisible to `git add`, which is
# exactly the failure documented at the top of this file.
!/scripts/
!/scripts/**

# Re-ignore generated, machine-specific and secret-bearing files. These come after the
# whitelist above because the last matching pattern wins.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS INTENDED FOR PUBLIC RELEASE. Nothing below describes someone's private
# infrastructure, credentials, or filesystem layout. Each has a committed .example twin.
#
# Structure dumps, generated credentials, filled bootstrap. Regenerate with seed-dev-db.ps1.
/tools/dev-db/.generated/**
# Names the operator's own live databases. See db-policy.example.json.
/tools/dev-db/db-policy.json
# Machine-specific paths and connection details. See dev-db.config.example.json.
/tools/dev-db/dev-db.config.json
# 01_bootstrap_root.sql is committed with __CHANGE_ME__ placeholders. If you fill them in,
# keep the filled copy out of the index.
/tools/dev-db/*.local.sql
# Records this machine's toolchain, DB inventory and security posture. Local only.
# See docs/setup.md for the shareable version.
/docs/environment.md
# Emitted changesets and their timestamped backups.
/out/changesets/**

# --- Hard re-ignores. Last matching pattern wins, so these override every `!` above. ---
#
# The whitelists above are broad (`!/src/**`, `!/bin/**`, `!/tests/**`), so an in-source build
# or a stray asset lands in a directory git is already looking inside. These two blocks close
# that. No currently tracked file matches any pattern here -- verified with `git ls-files`.
#
# 1. Build and editor artefacts. `/bin/**` in particular un-ignores a directory whose name
#    invites build output; nothing is tracked there today.
*.obj
*.o
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.tlog
*.user
*.suo
*.aps
#
# 2. WoW client data. NONE MAY EVER ENTER THIS REPOSITORY -- see ATTRIBUTION.md, "Blizzard
#    content". This is a copyright control, not tidiness: a single committed .blp is
#    redistribution of Blizzard assets and is permanent once pushed. Deliberately covers the
#    whole tree including tests/ and src/, so a fixture cannot be added without noticing.
*.mpq
*.MPQ
*.dbc
*.db2
*.m2
*.wmo
*.adt
*.wdt
*.wdl
*.blp
*.skin
*.anim
*.mdx
*.mdl
